  "meta": {
    "title": "The Longest Straight Line You Can Sail on Earth 🌊⛵🤯",
    "description": "What's the longest straight line you could sail without hitting land? ⛵ Scientists Rohan Chabukswar and Kushal Mukherjee confirmed it in 2018: start on the coast of Pakistan 🇵🇰, slip between Africa and Madagascar, pass between South America and Antarctica, cross the whole Pacific and land in Kamchatka, Russia 🇷🇺 That's about 32,090 km (19,940 miles) in one straight line 🤯",
    "pinnedComment": [
      "32,000 km in one straight line without touching land 🌊🤯",
      "Would you sail it? ⛵👇",
      "What should we measure next? 🗺️"
    ],
